# It sat alongside the other throwaway CI values (SECRET_KEY:
# test-secret-key-for-ci, POSTGRES_PASSWORD: test_password) and carried its own
# comment saying it was a throwaway needed only because the journal encryption
# tests require a real Fernet-format key.
#
# STATUS: NOT a live secret, confirmed rather than assumed. The value appears in
# no current tree - 0 occurrences on main and on feat/business-builder-canvas -
# is absent from .env.example and .env.production.example, and is referenced by
# no code or test on either branch. Adebayo confirmed on 2026-09-01 that no real
# journal data was ever encrypted with it, so there is nothing to rotate and no
# data to re-encrypt.
#
# WHY IT IS SUPPRESSED: the commit is published history. The value is already
# gone from every working tree; only the historical blob remains, and removing
# that needs git-filter-repo plus a force-push and a re-clone by everyone - a
# disproportionate response to a dead CI value.
#
# THE ACTUAL FIX SHIPPED ALONGSIDE THIS: the gitleaks step is now scoped with
# `--log-opts HEAD`. Before that, this single commit on ONE unmerged branch
# failed the job on every branch including main, because gitleaks scanned all
# refs rather than the branch under test.
#
# FOR THE FOUNDER-JOURNAL WORK, STILL IN FLIGHT: JOURNAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY must be
# supplied as a GitHub Actions secret referenced as ${{ secrets.* }}, never as
# an inline literal - see docs/deployment/GITHUB_ACTIONS_SETUP.md.
3ef75fef8eca7de5a0944525d30aa00a77eb87dc:.github/workflows/ci.yml:generic-api-key:81
